From: Yanghan Ye <yyh94306@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath12k: skip PPE direct switch for bridged VAPs

The QCN9274 PPE direct-switch path is a routed virtual-port datapath.  It
does not expose the VAP virtual ports as members of the PPE VSI flood
bitmaps, so using it for a VAP in a Linux bridge drops DHCP, ARP and other
unknown/broadcast traffic.  A VAP is commonly added to its bridge before
the vdev reaches the PPE attach point; leave that VAP on the normal
mac80211/Linux bridge path and keep direct switching available for
standalone routed VAPs.

Signed-off-by: Yanghan Ye <yyh94306@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/ppe.c | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/ppe.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/ppe.c
@@ -1,6 +1,7 @@
 // SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-3-Clause-Clear
 /* Qualcomm QCN9274 PPE direct-switch support. */
 
+#include <linux/if_bridge.h>
 #include <linux/dma-mapping.h>
 #include <linux/etherdevice.h>
 #include <linux/mm.h>
@@ -1235,5 +1235,10 @@ int ath12k_ppe_ds_vif_attach(struct ath12k_link_vif *arvif)
 	if (!ppe->started || !wdev || !wdev->netdev)
 		return 0;
+	/* PPE direct VPs cannot participate in the PPE VSI flood domain.
+	 * Keep bridged VAPs on the software bridge so DHCP and ARP work.
+	 */
+	if (netif_is_bridge_port(wdev->netdev))
+		return 0;
 	if (vif->type != NL80211_IFTYPE_AP &&
 	    vif->type != NL80211_IFTYPE_STATION)
 		return 0;
-- 
